        "abstract": "From 1953 to 1959 Gödel worked on a response to Carnap's philosophy of mathematics. The drafts display Gödel's familiarity with Carnap's position from The Logical Syntax of Language, but they received a dismissive reaction on their eventual, posthumous, publication. Gödel's two principal points, however, will here be defended. Gödel, though, had wished simply to append a few paragraphs to show that the same arguments apply to Carnap's later views. Carnap's position, however, had changed significantly in the intervening years, and to a significant extent, this mature position realizes much of what Gödel himself wanted out of a philosophy of mathematics.",
